Verify Backup in LocalStack

List Bucket

aws --endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566 s3 ls

List Backup Files

aws --endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566 \
s3 ls s3://velero-backups --recursive

Expected files

velero-backup.json

backup.tar.gz

logs.gz

resource-list.json.gz

results.gz

This proves the backup is physically stored in the S3 bucket.

Verify Existing Application

Before Disaster

kubectl get all -n microservices

Everything should be Running.

Disaster Simulation

Delete Entire Namespace

kubectl delete namespace microservices

Wait

kubectl get ns

Namespace disappears.

Verify Resources Gone

kubectl get all -n microservices

Expected

Namespace not found
Restore

Restore Backup

velero restore create \
--from-backup microservices-backup

Watch Restore

velero restore get

Expected

Completed

Detailed Restore

velero restore describe restore-xxxxx --details

Restore Logs

velero restore logs restore-xxxxx
